From 9dbb10eb10f4c7972667d574d00361639979bc50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huangserva <huangserva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:02:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] perf(sm70/tp2): fused NVFP4 residual epilogue, faster
 split reduce, MTP key window knob

- NVFP4 linear_add at decode widths: fp16-staged activation and residual
  add fused into the QPN epilogue (no projected temporary, no separate
  residual_add, one BF16 round). TP2 rank 1 writes its down-projection
  partial directly at T <= 32 instead of memset + linear_add.
- small-T split reduce: the idle 3/4 of the 256 threads (DChunk 64 for
  12/2) now share the split loop, branch-free and unrolled x8: 29 -> 13 us
  (T=4), 21 -> 9 us (T=1).
- NINFER_MTP_ATTN_WINDOW=W (default off): MTP draft attention over the last
  W keys only. Saves ~1.3 ms/round at 193K but code acceptance drops
  0.72 -> 0.59-0.63 (long-range structure), so it is not enabled.

TP2 e2e (256 tokens, temp 0.7): 186K code 100.4 tok/s, 193K zh 80.5
(acceptance 0.54 this sample; per round 32.5 ms), 8K code 140.2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
